<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n31724" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ob-lūdo</span></b> , si, sum, 3,
			v. n. * <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>To play off jokes</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">obludunt, qui custodem oblectent,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plaut. Truc. 1, 2, 10</span></i>
			.—* </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>To make sport of, mock</i> one; with <i>dat.</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">alicui,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Prud. Hamart. 6</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
